2) ADAPTIVE TIMESTEP
------------------------------------------------------------

Goal:
Each particle evolves on timestep appropriate to its
local dynamical time.

Add:

state[:, dt_index]

Define:

Class AdaptiveTimeStepController:

    METHOD compute_dt(state):

        For each particle:

            a = |acceleration|
            r = |position|

            local_dt_1 = eta * sqrt(softening / a)
            local_dt_2 = eta * r / |v|

            dt_i = min(local_dt_1, local_dt_2)

        Quantize to power-of-two hierarchy:

            dt_i = dt_min * 2^n

        Return dt_i array

Integrator modification:

    Use block timestep scheme:

        Global time loop:
            advance particles whose dt matches current time bin

This preserves symplectic structure if done carefully.

------------------------------------------------------------
3) MULTIPOLE EXPANSION TO QUADRUPOLE ORDER
------------------------------------------------------------

Current tree uses monopole only.

Upgrade node structure:

class OctreeNode:
    mass
    center_of_mass
    quadrupole_tensor (3x3 symmetric)
    half_size
    children

During tree build:

    For each node:

        Q_ij = Σ_k m_k *
               (3 x_i x_j - r_k^2 δ_ij)

Store symmetric 3x3 tensor.

Force evaluation:

If node accepted by opening criterion:

    r = x - COM
    d = |r|

    Monopole:
        a_mono = -G M r / d^3

    Quadrupole correction:
        a_quad_i = (G / (2 d^5)) *
                   Σ_j Q_ij r_j
                   - (5 G / (2 d^7)) *
                     (r^T Q r) r_i

Total:
    a = a_mono + a_quad

This reduces force error from O(θ^2)
to O(θ^4).

